   "claims": [
    "When prorated rent is applied, and you move into an apartment on the 20th of September (which has 30 days), your payment for this month would be one-third (10 / 30), i.e.",
    "Example of prorated rent calculation In the following example, let's make two assumptions: you move into a rented flat on the 15th of September, and the monthly rent is $650.",
    "Below, you can see a step-by-step guide on how to calculate the prorated rent: Move-in date: the 15th of September.",
    "Number of days of property occupancy: 16.",
    "Prorated rent: $21.6667 × 16 = $346.67 Remember to be very careful with calculating the number of days you will occupy the apartment in a month.",
    "Finally, your prorated rent in September is $346.67.",
    "If you moved on the 6th of June, the prorated rent would be 83.3% of the total monthly rent.",
    "Multiply the daily rent by the effective stay to find the prorated rent: prorated rent = monthly rent × 25/30 = monthly rent × 0.833.",
    "Thus the prorated rent is 83.3% of the monthly one."
   ],
